# NOTICE (English)

## What the license covers

Code and original written content in this repository are released under the MIT License — full text in [`LICENSE`](LICENSE). That includes the text we wrote under `translations/`.

## What `translations/` contains

The directory name is a holdover from early planning; its contents are not translations. Each entry is a summary and verification **written in our own words** after reading a third party's public benchmark, article, post or code — organizing their method and results, citing specific figures, linking the original, and weighing it against our own tests.

- No full text of the original is reproduced, and nothing is translated paragraph by paragraph; direct quotation is limited to short, attributed phrases.
- Each entry's `SOURCE.md` states its reproduction scope.
- Rights in the quoted material stay with its authors; the MIT License does not extend to it.

If an original author considers an entry beyond fair quotation, please open an issue and we'll revise or remove it.

## Contributing new entries

Write it up in your own words; don't paste in the original's full text or translate it paragraph by paragraph. If you must reproduce more than short phrases (e.g. full test items), first confirm the original license permits redistribution and record it in `SOURCE.md` — see [`CONTRIBUTING.md`](CONTRIBUTING.md).

## Other material

Public datasets used under `suites/` (e.g. PhysioNet/CinC Challenge 2015, ODC-By) are used under their original licenses; source and license are stated in each suite's README.

